            <div xml:id="d123">

                <pb facs="0205" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/656: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-12T17:00:00-04:00">June 12, 1934—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. Your despatch No. 567, June 2<anchor n="40" xml:id="d123-f1"/> and previous.
                    Have Cuban authorities now presented all their requests for concessions? If not,
                    please secure them at earliest opportunity and forward by air mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
